Done. One small improvement, committed.

**What I changed** (`src/commands_revisit.rs`):
• `contains_word()` claimed to be case-insensitive in its doc comment, but only lowercased the *text* — the *word* was matched verbatim. It worked only because the single call site (`is_shelved`) happened to pass pre-lowercased `SHELVED_LABELS`, which masked the contract mismatch (a latent bug for any future caller passing a mixed-case word).
• Fix: lowercase the word too (and use `word_lower.len()` for boundary arithmetic, so the byte offset stays consistent with the lowercased word).
• Added regression test `test_contains_word_case_insensitive_on_word_too` covering uppercase words, whole-word boundary enforcement with case, and empty-input behavior.

**Verification**: `cargo fmt` + `cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings` + `cargo build` clean; `cargo test` → 4301 passed / 1 ignored + 88 passed / 1 ignored. Committed as `ed6118c`. No doc updates needed — the fix makes the code match its existing doc comment, and no user-facing behavior changed.
